Package: RUMBLE
Type: Package
Title: Robust Unified Microbiome Biomarker Learning Engine
Version: 3.1.0
Authors@R: 
    person("Lucas", "Fett", email = "lucas.fett2021@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0009-0006-0596-3991"))
Description: RUMBLE (Robust Unified Microbiome Biomarker Learning Engine)
    implements a publication-quality consensus machine learning framework for
    identifying microbial biomarkers from high-throughput sequencing data.
    The package integrates multiple classification algorithms (Random Forest,
    XGBoost, Elastic Net, KNN) via the tidymodels ecosystem with nested
    cross-validation, and provides model-agnostic interpretability through
    SHAP values and permutation importance (via DALEX). It handles
    compositional microbiome data using multiplicative imputation
    (zCompositions::cmultRepl) followed by centered log-ratio (CLR)
    transformations with strict anti-leakage safeguards. Version 3.0
    introduces inter-fold stability assessment, feature selection frequency
    analysis, SHAP overfitting diagnostics (train vs test), hyperparameter
    stability reporting, cost-sensitive learning for class imbalance,
    Spearman-based directional metrics, and pooled out-of-fold ROC curves.
    Descriptive direction metrics replace statistically invalid p-values on
    SHAP correlations. Differential abundance integration with ANCOM-BC,
    ALDEx2, and Wilcoxon methods enables rigorous multi-evidence validation
    of biomarker candidates.
